T15b_live_verification_with_grants.instruction:
Goal: the live end-to-end check that T15 could not do (it failed only because the permissions were missing; read its report with atp-read-graph --view-mode local --node-id T15_live_verification). Prove Computer Use works the way Codex's does while the user keeps working in other apps.

Do NOT invalidate the grants: the grants belong to the exact installed helper build (ad-hoc signature = cdhash). Do not bump the helper version (PigCUHelperVersion / helperVersion in native/computer-use/Sources/Protocol.swift), do not ditto or reinstall anything into ~/.pi-gna/computer-use/, and do not run tccutil. `pnpm build:computer-use` only rewrites build/computer-use/ and is safe, because ComputerService reinstalls only when the bundled version is newer. If a check needs a helper fix, implement and test it with the directly spawned binary (inherits the terminal's grants, like scripts/computer-use-smoke.mjs --fixture does), commit it, and state in your report that the user must reinstall and re-grant; do not reinstall it yourself.

Steps:
1. pnpm build, then start a test instance with its own profile: PIGNA_USER_DATA=/tmp/pigna-cu-live PIGNA_BACKGROUND=1 node bin/pi-gna.mjs --remote-debugging-port=<free port> (see docs/DESIGN.md launch modes; never touch the user's running pi-gna). Drive the test instance's renderer through the remote debugging port (CDP) to enable Computer Use on its settings page and to send prompts to chats; or, if driving chats is impractical, exercise the same path below the UI: a script that starts ComputerService against the installed helper plus the /computer route, calling the extension's tool functions. Say which path you used.
2. Checks (with real apps, through the tools/route only):
   - permissions show as granted in the settings page or service;
   - TextEdit: new document via the tools, write a paragraph, select one word and replace it, read the state back;
   - Calculator: compute 12*34 by clicking buttons by element index, read the result;
   - screenshot of a TextEdit window that is covered by another window;
   - Terminal and pi-gna are refused; an app not yet allowed raises the approval (Allow once / Always allow / Deny behave as specified; answer approvals through CDP in the test instance);
   - two sessions drive TextEdit and Calculator at the same time; a second session on the same app gets the busy error;
   - the overlay cursor and pill appear above the target window and disappear when the run ends;
   - an action that cannot run in the background (e.g. on a minimized window) fails with background_unsupported instead of activating;
   - throughout: record NSWorkspace.frontmostApplication, the key window and NSEvent.mouseLocation before and after every action and confirm none changed;
   - transcript rendering of computer_* calls (summaries, AX details, screenshots) if you drove real chats.
3. Esc to cancel needs a real key press by the user: do not synthesize it. List it, with exact steps, as a manual check for the user in your report.
4. Fix small defects you find (minimal, tested, committed); report larger gaps with evidence.

Acceptance: every check in step 2 passes or has an evidenced gap in the report; pnpm test and pnpm typecheck pass; the grants still hold at the end (call the helper's permissions method and report the result).
